Below is a basic introduction to the notion of coupling. This is a
fundamental concept, with applications reaching into the study of
Markov processes and optimal transport problem. This overview will
be a simplistic coverage of what I see as the principal elements of
this topic.

#hr

A coupling of random variables (potentially on different probability
spaces) is another random variable whose marginal distributions are
equivalent in distribution to the original random variable. Of course,
a choice of a coupling random variable is non-unique. All ready you
can taste the flavor of the optimal transport problem, if you are
familiar with that area of study.

